<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="091" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT-2/4: the "To Do" tab — label, the blue Microsoft To Do check icon, tab spacing, Assigned To shows email, a clear confirmation and an Open-in-Spaarke link after creating</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 3 (2026-10-03)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies production `.tsx` in the task pane and BFF `.cs` (`OfficeSearchService` contact projection + its response DTO), with tests on both sides.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified UI adaptation plus one additive response field; every pattern copied from existing code.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>UAT3-W3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Wave W3, alone: it builds the BFF and edits `App.tsx` (092's in W1). Owns `TaskPaneToolbar.tsx`, `TaskPaneNavigation.tsx`, `CreateTodoView.tsx`, `App.tsx` (To Do + contact search handlers only), a new local icon file, and the BFF search code.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>088, 092, 093</deps>
    <tags>frontend, office-addins, typescript, bff-api, todo, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Owner UAT round 3 (2026-10-03), UAT-2: "Create To Do, change label to 'To Do'; use the blue check icon not the current icon; the Smart To Do (matches Microsoft To Do app icon); for the Assigned To pick include the person's email so can differentiate if multiple contact records; after saved need more obvious confirmation that the To Do was created; navigation link to open in Spaarke". UAT-4: "add space between the Save, Create To Do, Find". Record: `notes/042-uat-round3-2026-10-03.md` §1.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9) and the BFF Office search.</role>

  <goal>The pane's tab reads "To Do" with the blue Microsoft To Do check icon and the tabs are visibly spaced; a user picking an assignee sees each contact's email; after creating a To Do the user sees an unmistakable confirmation and can open it in Spaarke.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Tabs**: the rendered tab row is `TaskPaneToolbar.tsx:131-146` (size "small", no gap; bar styles 42-69); the
        label/icon come from `TaskPaneNavigation.tsx:100-104` (`'Create To Do'`, `TaskListAddRegular`). The toolbar
        announces the label (136-137). `TaskPaneNavigation`'s own styles (38-52) are dead — the component is not
        rendered (comment 18-26). Tests: `TaskPaneNavigation.test.tsx`, `TaskPaneShell.test.tsx`.
      - **Icon**: the Smart To Do surfaces use `MicrosoftToDoIcon` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/icons/MicrosoftToDoIcon.tsx:29-50`
        — the Microsoft To Do checkmark; `active` = brand blue), e.g. `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/components/KanbanHeader.tsx:36,169`.
        The add-in cannot import `@spaarke/ui-components`; copy the SVG into a local component (the precedent for a
        local copy is `FindResultsList.tsx:85-88`), with a comment naming the source file so the two can be kept in step.
      - **Assigned To**: `CreateTodoView.tsx:410-464` (rows: name + `displayInfo`, 439-458; chip: name only, 411-426).
        Search: `App.tsx` `handleSearchContacts` (449-484) → `GET /api/office/search/entities?q=…&amp;type=Contact&amp;top=10`,
        mapping id/name/displayInfo (471-478); `ContactOption` (`CreateTodoView.tsx:90-94`). Server: contact config
        `OfficeSearchService.cs:296` (`fullname` + `jobtitle`), selected columns 355-357, display text 405, DTO
        `EntitySearchResponse.cs:48-115` (its `PrimaryField` doc says "e.g., email for contacts", 87-91, but is set to
        the reference value or name at 406). Today a row reads "Attorney" (job title) or "contact" (none).
      - **After create**: `handleCreate` (`CreateTodoView.tsx:281-310`) sets `'created'`, shows a disabled gray "Saved"
        (514-518, style 200-204) and disables the fields (231). No message, no announcement, no link. The server
        returns 201 `{todoId, name}` (`OfficeEndpoints.cs:1430`; `Models/Office/CreateTodoRequest.cs:87-94`) but
        `App.handleCreateTodo` (398-446) returns `{ok:true}` and drops it; `CreateTodoResult` is `{ok, error}` (107-110).
      - **Open in Spaarke**: `openRecord({ entityType: 'sprk_todo', recordId })` via `openRecordLauncher` — which, after
        task 088, carries `appname` (the Spaarke app). Show it only with `canOpenBrowserWindow` and `ORG_URL`.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-03">Tab label exactly "To Do". The view heading may stay "Create a To Do"; its icon becomes the same blue check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Email is DISPLAY data: add `emailaddress1` to the contact projection and a dedicated response field (e.g. `secondaryText`/`email`), additive and optional; do NOT add it to the searched columns and do not repurpose `PrimaryField`'s existing value. Other entity types' responses are unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="security">The contact search keeps its existing per-user trim (task 062). The added column is read in the same query, under the same trim — no second query, no app-only read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 `MessageBar` (intent success) for the confirmation, semantic tokens, dark mode; the confirmation is also announced to screen readers (the pane's existing `useAnnounce`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10">The Open link is gated by capability, not host.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF obligations: placement stated; publish size vs a FRESH master build (Compress-Archive, equal file counts); CVE check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Client tests listed in `ci-gated-suites.txt`; server test in the existing Office search test class.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Do NOT edit 089's files (`WordAdapter.ts`, `adapters/types.ts`, `useSaveFlow.ts`, `word/commands/**`, `quickSaveHelpers.ts`, manifests, `packaging/**`, `webpack.config.js`, `word/taskpane/index.tsx`); they are done and out of scope.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The tab reads "To Do" with the blue check icon in both hosts; the screen-reader announcement says "To Do"; the updated tests pin it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The three tabs have visible spacing (a gap on the tab list); the tab bar does not wrap or clip at the pane's minimum width (320 px).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Assigned To search rows show name, and email when the contact has one (job title kept as a third, quieter line when present); the selected chip shows name and email. A contact with no email shows name only — no literal "contact".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Server: the contact search response carries the email field; a test asserts it is selected in the same query and that `emailaddress1` is not in the searched columns; non-contact responses are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After a successful create: a success MessageBar "To Do created: {name}" with an "Open in Spaarke" link that opens the new `sprk_todo` via `openRecord`; the confirmation is announced; with `canOpenBrowserWindow` false or no `ORG_URL`, the message shows without the link.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a failed create shows the server's reason (not only "Create failed (status)") and no success message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: gated jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production; Office search tests and ArchTests green; publish delta reported vs fresh master; CVE clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after a deploy): two contacts with the same name are told apart by email; creating a To Do shows the message and the link opens it in Matter Management. If unavailable, leave open and say so.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The contact search's per-user trim is applied in a way that adding a column to the projection would bypass (e.g. a second, app-only fetch) — STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the files in the background; confirm the 201 body shape and the search query path.</step>
    <step>Server: email in the contact projection + DTO field; test.</step>
    <step>Client: tab label/icon/spacing; contact rows and chip; `handleCreateTodo` returns `todoId`; confirmation + Open link; tests.</step>
    <step>Gates, publish size, conflict-check; record in `notes/091-todo-tab.md`; TASK-INDEX 091 → done.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>`MicrosoftToDoIcon` (shared library), the contact search route and DTO, the 201 body with `todoId`, `openRecordLauncher` and `useAnnounce` all exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a local copy of an existing icon, one additive response field, and wiring of data the server already returns. No new route or service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Users cannot tell same-named contacts apart and may assign a To Do to the wrong person record; a created To Do gives no visible confirmation and cannot be reached from the pane.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="To Do tab">
      <steps>
        <step>Open the pane in Word and Outlook: tabs "Save · To Do · Find", spaced, the To Do tab with the blue check.</step>
        <step>Assigned To: type a name shared by two contacts — each row shows its email.</step>
        <step>Create: a green confirmation with "Open in Spaarke"; the link opens the To Do in Matter Management.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Office dark theme: icon, rows and confirmation are readable.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

